	                              <p><a class="logo" href="/"><img alt="Southern Union State Community College" class="mb-4 mb-md-5" src="/img/suscc-logo-white.svg" /></a></p>

<p class="mb-4 mb-md-5">Southern Union State Community College, an open admission, public two-year college and member of the Alabama Community College System, provides quality and relevant teaching and learning in academic, technical, and health science programs that are affordable, accessible, equitable, and responsive to the diverse needs of its students, community, business, industry, and government.<br />
<br />
The mission of the&nbsp;Alabama Community College System (ACCS) is to provide a unified system of institutions that deliver academic education, adult education, and workforce development. The system focuses on offering accessible and affordable education to help students achieve their career and educational goals, benefiting individuals, communities, and the state&#39;s economy.<br />
<br />
SUSCC has adopted the <a href="https://www.accs.edu/about-accs/board-of-trustees/policies-and-procedures/" target="_blank">ACCS policies</a> as its institutional policies.<br />
Southern Union&#39;s <a href="/content/userfiles/files/26-SUSCC-1735_Strategic_Plan_Booklet-Revised-2%20(5).pdf" target="_blank">2026-2029 Strategic Plan</a></p>

<p class="text-white h5">Hours of Operation</p>

<ul>
	<li>Monday: 7:15AM - 4:30PM</li>
	<li>Tuesday: 7:15AM - 4:30PM</li>
	<li>Wednesday: 7:15AM - 4:30PM</li>
	<li>Thursday: 7:15AM - 4:30PM</li>
	<li>Friday: 7:15 AM - 12:15PM</li>
</ul>
